@startuml sd-conflict-resolution
skinparam shadowing false
title SD - Conflict resolution (last-writer-wins) when two instances update the same airport

participant "airports-routes-1" as A1
participant "RabbitMQ\nairports.events" as MQ
participant "airports-routes-2" as A2

== Concurrent updates of the same airport ==
A1 -> A1 : PATCH /api/airports/OPO/status\nlastModified = T1, originNodeId = airports-routes-1
A2 -> A2 : PATCH /api/airports/OPO/status\nlastModified = T2, originNodeId = airports-routes-2

A1 -> MQ : AIRPORT_STATUS_CHANGED (T1)
A2 -> MQ : AIRPORT_STATUS_CHANGED (T2)

MQ -> A1 : event from airports-routes-2 (T2)
MQ -> A2 : event from airports-routes-1 (T1)
note over MQ
  The fanout also returns each instance its own
  event: the consumer ignores events whose
  originNodeId equals its own node id.
end note

== Decision on each instance: isNewer(incoming, current) ==
A1 -> A1 : T2 > T1 ?\nyes -> apply (airports-routes-2 wins)
A2 -> A2 : T1 > T2 ?\nno -> ignore (own state is newer)

note over A1, A2
  Rule: the update with the later lastModified wins.
  On a tie, the larger originNodeId wins.
  Both instances converge to the same state
  (eventual consistency). Events are idempotent:
  applying the same event twice changes nothing.
end note
@enduml
